course: dictionary
lesson: 693
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can mean different things in different places. «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang shows whether the storm is coming closer or moving away.» Here a bang is a sudden, very loud noise, like the crack of thunder after lightning.
explain: The same word can also be an action. «At the zoo Kieran bangs on the monkey glass» means he hits the glass hard, so it makes a loud noise. Look at the words around bang to decide whether it is a thing or an action.
explain: Some phrases have their own meaning. «Bang on time» means exactly on time, and it is informal, so you would not use it in a formal letter. When the context is not enough, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A bang is a sudden, very loud noise, like an explosion or a door slamming.
fact: Bang can be a noun, a verb or an adverb, so the words around it show which one it is.
fact: Sound travels about 1 kilometre in 3 seconds, so counting from flash to bang tells you how far away lightning is.
fact: In America, bangs are hair cut short and straight across the forehead. In Britain this is called a fringe.
fact: The Big Bang is the scientists' name for how the universe began.
exercise: «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang shows whether the storm is coming closer.» In this sentence, what is a bang? | A hair style with a fringe | A slow, quiet whisper | A kind of bright light | *A sudden, very loud noise
exercise: «At the zoo Kieran bangs on the monkey glass.» What is Kieran doing? | *Hitting the glass hard | Hugging the glass | Cleaning the glass gently | Looking at the monkeys quietly
exercise: Dad says, «We must leave at nine, bang on time.» What does bang on mean? | Slowly and carefully | *Exactly on time | Early, before anyone is ready | Very late
test: In «go off with a bang», what does the phrase mean? | Fall over on the floor | Stop working suddenly | *Be very successful | Make a loud noise by accident
test: Where is «bangs» used to mean a fringe on the forehead? | In Britain | *In America | In every country in the same way | In science lessons only
exam: In «On a beach in Florida, a boy counts 12 seconds from flash to bang», about how far away is the lightning? | About 12 kilometres | About 1 kilometre | *About 4 kilometres
